From 9e0080defb4d906f181ff22baa2633c717c7517a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atjiki1 <atjiki1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:22:43 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 8/8] notifications/ancs: keep one copy and name the secondary
 device

With CONFIG_BT_MULTI_LINK_EXPERIMENT, the phone and the secondary device
often post the same notification (iMessage, apps signed in on both):

- Remember a hash of app id, title, subtitle and message of the last
  notifications for 30 s. A copy from the other device is dropped, so
  the watch alerts once. When the secondary device's copy came first,
  the phone's copy replaces it without a new alert, so dismissing and
  other actions go to the phone.
- Show the secondary device's stored name in the subtitle of its
  notifications, after their own subtitle if they have one.

ANCS_SECONDARY_UID_FLAG moves to ancs.h for this.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 pebble/comm/ble/kernel_le_client/ancs/ancs.c  |   6 +-
 pebble/comm/ble/kernel_le_client/ancs/ancs.h  |   3 +
 .../notifications/ancs/ancs_notifications.c   | 196 +++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 199 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

